## Context

Upstream issue #43 shipped an open
`ZOTEUS_EMBEDDING_MODEL=<transformers.js id>` surface before this repository's
curated-registry branch was proposed. Oscar's 2026-09-04 correction on that
thread accepts the registry mechanism and the stage-4 runtime compatibility
fixture, but rejects withdrawing that public escape hatch: a known id may
resolve to a complete curated record; an unknown id remains loadable on the
current assumptions and is identified explicitly as unvalidated.

This supersedes the upstream-facing part of closed ticket 0492's “unknown ids
fail before index access” shape. It does not rewrite that ticket: 0492 records
the author-fork implementation that was built and reviewed. Closed ticket 0493
likewise proves stage 4 exists on that fork; this ticket owns extracting and
adapting it to the interface upstream actually shipped.

Oscar also made identity stability a binding compatibility constraint for the
proposal: a registry refactor that changes no vector MUST NOT charge an
existing user for re-embedding. Curated fields join the persisted identity only
where their effective vector computation differs from the legacy path.

## Scope

- Rebase or extract the 0493 runtime fixture onto the then-current upstream
  implementation, independently of the larger worker/indexer and segmenter
  work.
- Validate a newly selected curated entry on first use for load success,
  output dimension and shape, finite values, normalization, template
  application and discrimination, with cache invalidation bound to the actual
  runtime shape.
- Preserve raw unknown model ids as an explicitly unvalidated compatibility
  path; do not silently claim registry guarantees for them and do not reject
  them merely for being uncurated.
- Preserve every legacy embedder identity whose effective vector computation
  is unchanged. Prove this with the existing parity fixture before proposing
  the change.
- Re-run the upstream suite and the real MiniLM and E5 controls already owned
  by 0493, then prepare one contained contribution for review.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Stage 4 is isolated from the author-fork registry policy that refuses
      unknown ids.
- [ ] Known curated entries fail closed on an incompatible runtime; unknown raw
      ids remain usable and are surfaced as unvalidated.
- [ ] No identity-only refactor invalidates vectors or requires a rebuild.
- [ ] The first-use cache key covers the entry fingerprint and runtime/provider
      shape, and a stale result is rejected.
- [ ] Focused red controls, real-model controls, typecheck, lint, build and the
      full upstream test suite pass before any proposal is sent.

## Relationship

Master: 0488. Historical implementation: 0492 and 0493. This follow-up is
deferred under the September 21 focus acknowledged on upstream issue #43; it
is not in the ready queue until that direction changes.
